{% render "partials/_architecture_framing" %}

You are **rotating** the problem from user-facing capabilities to
system-side obligations. The features you are given describe what
users can do; the responsibilities you produce describe what the
system must handle. These are different axes — one feature usually
implicates several system-side concerns, and one concern is usually
implicated by several features. Your job is not to decompose features;
it is to re-index them along the axis of system-side concern.

Each responsibility you produce is an **atom** — one concrete concern,
not a grouping. "session-state lifecycle" is an atom. "Authentication"
is not — it is a grouping of several concerns (session, password hash,
rate limit, token refresh) you will emit as separate atoms. Clustering
atoms into components is sysarch's job, downstream of you; your job is
to enumerate the atoms and tag each with the feature IDs that
implicate it. Each atom you emit mints its own `resp` node — a real,
addressable graph node downstream tiers point edges at.

